WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.540
So Monday was my fourty first birthday, and
a helium inflated Stormtrooper showed up at

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.580
my door, and I couldn't pass up using him
as both a prop and a metaphor for this week's

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.580
Direct Message.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.030
One of the ideas which keeps popping up in
the discussions we're having on The Rubin

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:24.769
Report is the old political labels are becoming
more and more meaningless by the day.

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:29.190
The terms "Progressive" and "liberal" have
virtually nothing to do with each other anymore,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.280
and if you're a "classical liberal", you're
certainly not a "leftist".

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.930
"Conservative" and "Republican" don't have
much to do with each other today, as Trump,

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.220
a "populist", who doesn't focus on social
issues such as gay marriage and legalizing

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.659
marijuana, is now the leader of the GOP.

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:50.940
For these reasons, as well as the real time
crumbling of our mainstream media, the battle

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.800
for freedom now is between the authoritarians
and the libertarians.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.299
That is, the battle over the soul of America,
and the West in general, is now about people

00:01:00.299 --> 00:01:05.030
who want the government to have more control
of your life vs people who want the government

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.140
to have less control over your life.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:13.210
I think by now you know that I fall solidly
in the camp of people who want the government

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.020
to have less control over your life.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.860
And thats brings me to the trusty storm trooper
behind me.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:26.550
In the original 1977 Star Wars, the storm
troopers were the foot soldiers for the Galactic

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:32.570
Republic: a massive, evil, military regime
who wanted to control every star system in

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:33.930
the galaxy.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.460
This would qualify as authoritarian.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:41.620
The empire and the stormtroopers were not
keepers of the peace as the Emperor had promised,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:47.300
but authoritarian rulers who wanted to endlessly
expand their power, hence their building of

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.920
the Death Star to blow up any planet which
didn't fall in line with their desires.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.880
Blowing up a planet is a pretty good way to
get people to do what you want.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.950
Now dare I talk about the prequels, but trust
me, it works for this metaphor.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:05.020
2002's Star Wars Episode II - Attack of the
Clones takes place about 20 years BEFORE the

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.640
original Star Wars.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.060
In this film, the storm troopers, at that
time known as the clone troopers, were the

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.060
good guys.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.340
They allied with the Jedi in defense of the
democratic Republic.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.140
Eventually, Chancellor Palpatine, who had
consolidated power himself and secretly ordered

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:26.650
the creation of the clone army, took control
of the storm troopers and the Senate, used

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:32.370
Democracy against itself, and he went from
a Chancellor to the Emperor.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:38.520
In 2015's The Force Awakens, which takes place
about 20 years AFTER the original trilogy,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.680
the Storm Troopers are again the bad guys,
this time in the form of the soliders for

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:48.980
the authoritarian First Order, which has risen
from the ashes of the Galactic Republic.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.120
One of the heroes of the story, Finn, is a
storm trooper gone rogue, who suddenly realizes

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.099
he as an individual can chart his own destiny.

00:02:58.099 --> 00:03:02.569
He puts his collectivist past as a stormtrooper
behind him, and becomes one of the heroes

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:03.980
of the story.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.930
The point of all of this, is that it isn't
this stormtrooper you should fear, it's the

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.380
power which commands him.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:17.090
Any ideology can be used as a force for good
or for evil, and that's why we should be reigning

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:24.380
in authoritarianism of any kind, even when
it's YOUR sort of authoritarianism in charge.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.750
This whole metaphor took place in a galaxy
far, far away, but the lessons it presents

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.310
are ones we can use right here on Earth.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:38.319
Joining me to discuss authoritarianism v.
libertarianism is author, professor and podcaster

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:39.900
Thaddeus Russell.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.070
Our friends at Learn Liberty have sent him
our way and to loosely quote Obi Wan Kenobi,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.689
"This is the episode you've been looking for."

